                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_59">Bordesley,
                        Worcestershire. Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>'Iste
                        liber constat Iohanni Norpewode monacho . qui ipsum habuerit. vel qui in eo
                        legerit habeat eum karitatiue specialiter recommendatum in missa sua priuata
                        commemoracione. vel saltem oret pro anima eius . Et quicumque hunc librum ab
                        eo alienauerit absque eius licencia: malediccionem dei incurrat . fiat fiat.
                        Amen.' (fol. 183r).</p><p>Inscription, with illuminated border, recording
                        the first owner's noviciate: 'Anno domini Milesimo CCC. octogesimo sexto. In
                        die sancti Augustini Anglorum apostoli [26 May]. Intrauit domum probacionis
                        beate Marie de Bordesley frater Johannes Norþewode, quem in uia religionis
                        assumpte deuotissime custodiat trinitas sancta nunc et in perpetuum. amen.'
                        (fol. 182v).</p><p> Original binding of oak boards covered with red
                        vellum.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">'Iste lyber pertinet ad me mi lady Peyto.
                     Amen yt est yta fyat amen so be heyte... by the, gefte of d[ame?] Goodyth Peyto
                     thy booke Goody Thokmarton' (fol. 2r, s. xvi early).</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Goditha, daughter of Sir Thomas Throckmorton,
                     was wife of Edward Peto (d. 1487) and mother of Cardinal William
                     Peto.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">T. S. Walker.</provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Lord Amherst of Hackney, no. 23. Sold
                     Sothebys 25 March 1909, lot 643.</provenance>
